  "symbol_provenance": {
    "description": "Every routine and data label comes from the surviving source. The two resource-block labels identify the added header boundary. Names containing __local_ are verifier names for original @ labels under their preceding global label. The byte comparison establishes label addresses but does not establish the spelling used by the lost 1985 source revision.",
    "resource_entry_reference": "_PACK_5_ at 0x41cf2e"
  },
  "changes": [
    {
      "kind": "resource_wrapper",
      "description": "Added the eight-byte block header before ELEMS68K. Its size is PACK5ResourceEnd-PACK5ResourceBlock. Preserved the original body header, including version one."
    },
    {
      "kind": "package_locking",
      "description": "Restored ROMRSRC to zero by reactivating the earlier definition already present in the driver. Preserved the later definition as a comment. The entry saves the state byte from the PACK 5 handle, sets lock bit seven, and restores the state before returning. Both code paths remain under the original conditionals."
    },
    {
      "kind": "source_structure",
      "description": "Kept the original driver and four implementation includes as separate active files. Replaced the compiled StandardEqu.d dependency with selected interface equates and macros in ElemsSANEMacs.a. Include names now match the saved filenames. No arithmetic routine, special-case path, dispatch entry or constant was removed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "macros",
      "description": "Retained 32 active SANE macros from SANEMacs.a. Their calls still express floating arithmetic, comparisons, conversions, exception handling and environment changes. FADDX uses CLR.W -(SP) to emit the ROM selector zero; the released macro writes zero with MOVE.W #FFEXT+FOADD,-(SP). Every other selected macro body remains unchanged. Trap _FP68K uses its named OPWORD value $A9EB."
    },
    {
      "kind": "addressing",
      "description": "Added explicit PC addressing to 77 existing code or data references. These are PEA and LEA operands and the ELEMSTAB/LIFTOFF indexed dispatch operands. The labels and targets remain unchanged."
    },
    {
      "kind": "branch_encoding",
      "description": "Selected the observed short encoding at nine branches in Elems68K2.a. Seven unsized processor branches now use .S. The annuity tests use existing FBULTS and FBEQS macros in place of the long variants. The conditions and targets remain unchanged."
    },
    {
      "kind": "comments_and_history",
      "description": "Preserved the original comments and history in all five source files. The reconstruction notes identify these later headers as provenance. Elems68K3.a retains a later header that names the MC68881; this ROM implementation calls the software FP68K package. Later dates, placeholder header fields and original comment errors remain as released source text."
    }
  ],
